(VAL-08: bare arithmetic on a value is a compile error — a value's type is
 only known at runtime, so `v add 1` inside a value-parameter function is
 rejected at compile time. (Compile-error claim: not assertable from a
 runtime leaf, since emitting it produces a non-compiling program — outside
 the generator's "legal Vox that should compile and run" contract.)
